Enable shared memory in Fast DDS's builtin (default) transports.

Upstream's CMake build defines SHM_TRANSPORT_BUILTIN by default
(SHM_TRANSPORT_DEFAULT=ON), which adds the shared memory transport to the
default transports next to UDPv4. The RCR's Bazel build doesn't, so ROS
processes on the same machine talked over UDP loopback only (no shared memory
segments were created). FASTDDS_BUILTIN_TRANSPORTS=DEFAULT?... in .bazelrc then
gives shared memory + UDPv4 as upstream intends.

--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -98,5 +98,6 @@
     }),
     local_defines = [
+        "SHM_TRANSPORT_BUILTIN",
         "USE_THIRDPARTY_SHARED_MUTEX=1",
     ] + select({
         "@platforms//os:windows": ["WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN"],
